en-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Superagonistic anti-CD28 antibodies: potent activators of regulatory T cells for the therapy of autoimmune diseases.</article-title><source>Ann Rheum Dis</source><volume>64</volume><issue>Suppl 4</issue><fpage>iv91</fpage><lpage>iv95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16239397</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001708-Beyersdorf3"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beyersdorf</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanke</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerkau</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunig</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>CD28 superagonists put a break on autoimmunity by preferentially activating CD4&#x0002b;CD25&#x0002b; regulatory T cells.</article-title><source>Autoimmun Rev</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>40</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16338210</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001708-Beyersdorf4"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beyersdorf</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Balbach</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunig</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerkau</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Large-scale expansion of rat CD4&#x0002b; CD25&#x0002b; T(reg) cells in the absence of T-cell receptor stimulation.</article-title><source>Immunology</source><volume>119</volume><fpage>441</fpage><lpage>450</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16903867</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001708-Lin1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name